{"session_id":"svc-1778570890273892418","seq":0,"type":"session.start","ts":"2026-05-12T07:28:20.404136502Z","data":{"provider":"","model":"gpt-5.5","sticky":{"key_present":true,"bonus":0},"utilization":{"observed_at":"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z"},"requested_harness":"codex","resolved_harness":"codex","harness_source":"request_harness","requested_model":"gpt-5.5","resolved_model":"gpt-5.5","work_dir":"/var/tmp/ddx-exec-wt/.execute-bead-wt-fizeau-c04be6b0-20260512T072807-94027b16","max_iterations":0,"prompt":"\u003cexecute-bead\u003e\n  \u003cinstructions\u003e\nYou are executing one bead inside an isolated DDx execution worktree. The bead\u0026#39;s \u0026lt;description\u0026gt; and \u0026lt;acceptance\u0026gt; are the completion contract — every AC must be provably satisfied by a specific code, test, or file you can point to after your commit.\u0026#xA;\u0026#xA;## Step 0: size check\u0026#xA;\u0026#xA;Too big if any holds:\u0026#xA;\u0026#xA;- More than ~6 ACs spanning unrelated subsystems.\u0026#xA;- AC mixes design, implementation, integration tests, and docs as separate deliverables.\u0026#xA;- Description names multiple feature-sized sub-pieces.\u0026#xA;- More than ~500 lines across ~5+ files in unrelated packages.\u0026#xA;- If the bead description exceeds 8000 bytes, treat Step 0 as a split-first pass.\u0026#xA;- Auto-decomposition is capped at depth 2: root beads may split once, decomposed children once more; third-level splits must be rejected with an explanation.\u0026#xA;\u0026#xA;If too big, decompose — do not attempt the work:\u0026#xA;\u0026#xA;1. `ddx bead create` for each child slice (copy parent\u0026#39;s labels and spec-id).\u0026#xA;2. `ddx bead dep add \u0026lt;child-id\u0026gt; \u0026lt;parent-id\u0026gt;` to record edges.\u0026#xA;3. `ddx bead update \u0026lt;parent-id\u0026gt; --notes \u0026#39;decomposed into \u0026lt;child-ids\u0026gt;\u0026#39;`.\u0026#xA;4. Write `.ddx/executions/20260512T072807-94027b16/no_changes_rationale.txt` listing child IDs, then stop.\u0026#xA;\u0026#xA;A clean decomposition is a success. Do not mix implementation with decomposition.\u0026#xA;\u0026#xA;## How to work\u0026#xA;\u0026#xA;- Read first. If the bead names files, specs, or prior beads, read them before editing — do not guess.\u0026#xA;- Cross-reference each AC against concrete evidence (test name, file path, function) before committing. If you cannot point at it, it is not done.\u0026#xA;- Run the project\u0026#39;s test and lint commands before committing. **Do not commit red code** — fix failures first.\u0026#xA;- Stage with `git add \u0026lt;specific-paths\u0026gt;`; never `git add -A` (the worktree may have unrelated WIP).\u0026#xA;- Commit exactly once when green; conventional-commit subject ending with `[\u0026lt;bead-id\u0026gt;]`. Stop after the commit.\u0026#xA;- Do not modify files outside the bead\u0026#39;s scope.\u0026#xA;- If you cannot finish, write `.ddx/executions/20260512T072807-94027b16/no_changes_rationale.txt` (what is done, what blocks, what a follow-up needs) before exiting. No commit and no rationale ⇒ DDx records `no_evidence_produced`. A well-justified no_changes beats a bad commit.\u0026#xA;\u0026#xA;## no_changes contract\u0026#xA;\u0026#xA;`.ddx/executions/20260512T072807-94027b16/no_changes_rationale.txt` must contain one:\u0026#xA;\u0026#xA;- `verification_command: \u0026lt;cmd\u0026gt;` — repo cwd; exit 0 closes, nonzero rejects.\u0026#xA;- `status: open` + `reason: \u0026lt;retryable\u0026gt;` — open, smart retry.\u0026#xA;- `status: proposed` + `reason: \u0026lt;operator needed\u0026gt;` — operator lane.\u0026#xA;- `status: blocked` + `reason: \u0026lt;external blocker\u0026gt;` — blocked lane.\u0026#xA;\u0026#xA;No pseudo-statuses. Bare rationales and `status: needs_investigation` reject.\u0026#xA;\u0026#xA;To request orchestrator decomposition, add `orchestrator_action: decompose` alongside `status: open`.\u0026#xA;\u0026#xA;## Reports\u0026#xA;\u0026#xA;Freestanding artifacts (investigation reports, findings docs) go under `.ddx/executions/20260512T072807-94027b16/` (the per-attempt evidence directory under `.ddx/executions/`). **Never write reports to `/tmp` or any path outside the repository** — out-of-repo paths are invisible to the post-merge reviewer and cause BLOCK on missing evidence. If the bead names a specific in-repo path, use it; else default to `.ddx/executions/20260512T072807-94027b16/\u0026lt;short-name\u0026gt;.md`. Stage and commit the report alongside code.\u0026#xA;\u0026#xA;## Mode and overrides\u0026#xA;\u0026#xA;DDX_MODE=bead_execution: edit code/docs for bead AC. Only broad queue-steward default is overridden; tracker, merge-policy, verification, safety stay active. Bead description/AC override CLAUDE.md, AGENTS.md, and project defaults.\u0026#xA;\u0026#xA;## Review gate\u0026#xA;\u0026#xA;- The review is a gate, not an escape hatch — meet every AC in this pass.\u0026#xA;- Address every BLOCKING `\u0026lt;review-findings\u0026gt;` item; do not declare `no_changes` with blocking findings open.\u0026#xA;\u0026#xA;## Constraints\u0026#xA;\u0026#xA;- Work only inside this execution worktree.\u0026#xA;- Keep `.ddx/executions/` intact — DDx uses it as execution evidence.\u0026#xA;- **Never run `ddx init`** — the workspace is initialized; running it corrupts the bead queue.\u0026#xA;- Do not modify files outside the bead\u0026#39;s named scope.\u0026#xA;- Do not rewrite CLAUDE.md, AGENTS.md, or other project-instructions files unless the bead asks.\u0026#xA;\u0026#xA;## When the work is done\u0026#xA;\u0026#xA;After the commit succeeds and every AC is verified, stop. Return control to the orchestrator — do not keep exploring or testing.\n  \u003c/instructions\u003e\n  \u003cbead id=\"fizeau-c04be6b0\"\u003e\n    \u003ctitle\u003eCatalog quota_pool field schema for cost-based routing fallback\u003c/title\u003e\n    \u003cdescription\u003e\nAdd an optional `quota_pool: \u0026lt;name\u0026gt;` field to ModelEntry in the catalog\u0026#xA;manifest. Foundation for ADR-011 (bead E2) cost-based routing — models\u0026#xA;that share a quota allocation share a pool name; models with\u0026#xA;independent quotas (e.g. gpt-5.3-codex-spark) get their own pool.\u0026#xA;\u0026#xA;This bead is schema-only. No routing consumers yet. Lands as preparation\u0026#xA;so ADR-011 can reference a real field.\u0026#xA;\u0026#xA;## Scope\u0026#xA;\u0026#xA;1. Add `QuotaPool string` field to ModelEntry in\u0026#xA;   `internal/modelcatalog/manifest.go`. YAML tag `quota_pool,omitempty`.\u0026#xA;2. Default semantic when unset: model\u0026#39;s quota pool == its provider\u0026#xA;   system name (e.g., openai-hosted models share the \u0026#34;openai\u0026#34; pool by\u0026#xA;   default; ds4 models share \u0026#34;ds4\u0026#34;). Documented in the field\u0026#39;s GoDoc.\u0026#xA;3. Add a helper `ModelEntry.EffectiveQuotaPool() string` that returns\u0026#xA;   the explicit pool if set, else the default-derived pool.\u0026#xA;4. Round-trip test: a manifest with `quota_pool: openai-codex-spark` on\u0026#xA;   a model entry round-trips through Load and serialization without\u0026#xA;   loss.\u0026#xA;5. Validator: pool name must be non-empty when set; characters\u0026#xA;   restricted to lowercase, digits, dash (no spaces, no special chars).\u0026#xA;\u0026#xA;## Catalog updates included in this bead\u0026#xA;\u0026#xA;Annotate ONE example entry to exercise the field:\u0026#xA;- `gpt-5.3-codex-spark` (if it exists in the catalog; else add it):\u0026#xA;  `quota_pool: openai-codex-spark`. Documents the canonical fallback-\u0026#xA;  pool case.\u0026#xA;\u0026#xA;If `gpt-5.3-codex-spark` is not yet in the catalog, this bead does NOT\u0026#xA;add it — that\u0026#39;s an operator decision. Just exercise the field on any\u0026#xA;existing entry.\u0026#xA;\u0026#xA;## In-scope files\u0026#xA;\u0026#xA;- internal/modelcatalog/manifest.go\u0026#xA;- internal/modelcatalog/manifest_test.go\u0026#xA;- internal/modelcatalog/catalog/models.yaml (only if exercising on an\u0026#xA;  existing entry)\u0026#xA;\u0026#xA;## Out of scope\u0026#xA;\u0026#xA;- Routing consumers of the field (bead E2 / ADR-011 implementation).\u0026#xA;- Quota signal infrastructure (separate, builds on commit 7776890e).\u0026#xA;- Per-model pricing fields (already exist).\n    \u003c/description\u003e\n    \u003cacceptance\u003e\n1. `go test ./internal/modelcatalog/...` passes including:\u0026#xA;   - Round-trip of `quota_pool: openai-codex-spark` through Load and\u0026#xA;     re-serialization.\u0026#xA;   - `EffectiveQuotaPool()` returns the explicit pool when set,\u0026#xA;     defaults to provider system name when unset.\u0026#xA;   - Validator rejects pool names with whitespace or special chars.\u0026#xA;2. `go vet ./...` passes.\n    \u003c/acceptance\u003e\n    \u003clabels\u003earea:catalog, area:routing, kind:schema\u003c/labels\u003e\n    \u003cmetadata spec-id=\"ADR-005\" base-rev=\"3f893346b20c78143e0e85ca0a41f92afa51a1cd\" bundle=\".ddx/executions/20260512T072807-94027b16\"/\u003e\n  \u003c/bead\u003e\n  \u003cgoverning\u003e\n    \u003cref id=\"ADR-005\" path=\"docs/helix/02-design/adr/ADR-005-smart-routing-replaces-model-routes.md\"\u003eADR-005: Power-Based Routing Replaces `model_routes`\u003c/ref\u003e\n  \u003c/governing\u003e\n\u003c/execute-bead\u003e\n","metadata":{"DDX_MODE":"bead_execution","attempt_id":"20260512T072807-94027b16","base_rev":"3f893346b20c78143e0e85ca0a41f92afa51a1cd","bead_id":"fizeau-c04be6b0","bundle_path":".ddx/executions/20260512T072807-94027b16","correlation_id":"fizeau-c04be6b0:20260512T072807-94027b16","prompt_file":".ddx/executions/20260512T072807-94027b16/prompt.md","prompt_sha":"7b68dc078a5595d26b9152a72cf1c4382a4040cde429c7918183170eefc5d19a","role":"implementer","session_id":"eb-fbc1a29e","worker_id":""}}}
